# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# Cross-origin isolation enables SharedArrayBuffer, which ONNX Runtime Web's
# WASM execution provider needs for multi-threaded inference (issue #45). Without
# these headers the WASM AI fallback (no-WebGPU devices) runs single-threaded and
# is much slower.
#
# COEP: require-corp means every cross-origin subresource must opt in via CORP or
# CORS. The AI model is fetched from R2 with `mode: "cors"`, so the R2 bucket must
# return `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` (or `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy:
# cross-origin`). The ORT wasm/glue assets are served same-origin from /ort/, so
# they are unaffected.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
